Hi Arthur,

I am confused, as the report output is to my understanding speaking about distances in the 2nd and 4th column and not SNPs. The report above is not filtering from intially 422808660 SNPs (that would be too many anyways)
the 9196 SNPs at a 0.25 treshold. These must be distances right? Please find below the object before and after the hamming filtering, as you see 5070 SNPs got removed, an absolute SNP number which is not stated in the report, only distances.So why does the report say that 100 % loci are retained, when in fact 5070 loci are removed?

Also, I guess you made a typo, 0.25 is 4 or less bases and 0.20 is 5 or less :).

Kind regards,
Flo

